[ti:Amazing Grace]
[ar:John Newton (1779)]
[length:02:10]
[by:SingLearn - Nhom 10 (auto-aligned, faster-whisper)]
[00:06.70]Amazing grace! How sweet the sound
[00:14.86]That saved a wretch like me!
[00:24.88]I once was lost, but now am found,
[00:35.28]Was blind, but now I see.
[00:45.70]'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear,
[00:56.38]And grace my fears relieved;
[01:07.04]How precious did that grace appear
[01:16.78]The hour I first believed.
[01:27.64]When we've been there ten thousand years,
[01:37.16]Bright shining as the sun,
[01:47.76]We've no less days to sing God's praise
[01:57.72]Than when we'd first begun.
[02:05.22]
